From: TensorFold recipe <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] dsv41 lanes: a long prompt pass lets the streams already live decode between its chunks, and answers their cancels (TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD)

Rationale (issue #3 of this recipe): a prompt pass ran to completion inside its admission, so a stream that was decoding got no token
until the pass returned (90 s for a 120K-token cold prompt, measured), and a cancel posted meanwhile waited for it. Now the backend
offers the host a stop between two chunks (Stream.yield, never after the last: the prompt's logits sit in the chunk workspace); the
host runs up to TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD decode rounds for the live streams, delivers their tokens and takes every cancel but the pass's own
(which the pass sees between chunks as before). Around the rounds the backend joins the next chunk's Engram read-ahead and hides the
fill's ids, as the follower already does for any frame but a chunk; rank 1 follows rank 0's frames in order and re-points the ids at
its next chunk. Rank 0 only reads the switch. Prompts with images do not yield.

Switch: TF_DS_PREFILL_YIELD=N (rounds per stop, at most 64; unset or 0 = OFF: the pinned behaviour, no frame changes).
Adds a host test (a fake backend that offers the stop between chunks): with the switch on a live stream decodes during the pass
and its cancel is answered inside it; off, it does neither.

Written for this recipe; no code copied from other projects.
---
